NEARS-422 AC5 cross-module deep-link — STILL FAILS (fix-cycle 1)

Repro: app active in Grocery(module 1)/zone 2 Abu Dhabi. Fired deep link to a
PHARMACY (module 3) item 598:
  https://6ammart-web.6amtech.com/item-details/multivitamin-daily-53?id=598&page=item&module=pharmacy

Live logcat (full query params confirmed delivered to the app):
  I flutter : Received Deep Link URI: https://6ammart-web.6amtech.com/item-details/multivitamin-daily-53?id=598&page=item&module=pharmacy
  I flutter : =======Navigating to item details route: /item-details/multivitamin-daily-53?id=598&page=item&module=pharmacy
  I flutter : ====> API Response: [404] /api/v1/items/details/598

Result: item 404s -> fail-safe 'item_not_found' fires, nothing pushed, screen
stays on the prior grocery store-profile. The cross-module item NEVER resolves.

Backend proof the item is fine, the MODULE CONTEXT is wrong:
  GET /api/v1/items/details/598  moduleId:3 (pharmacy) zoneId:[2]  -> HTTP 200
  GET /api/v1/items/details/598  moduleId:1 (grocery)  zoneId:[2]  -> HTTP 404
  GET /api/v1/items/details/598  (no module header)               -> HTTP 403

Root cause (link_converter_helper.dart openItemDeepLink):
  final int? deepLinkModuleId = int.tryParse(moduleId);   // moduleId == "pharmacy" -> null
  if (deepLinkModuleId != null) { await forcefullySetModule(deepLinkModuleId); }  // SKIPPED
  await itemController.getItemDetails(itemId: itemId, ...); // runs against stale GROCERY module -> 404

The deep-link `module` query param is the module NAME ("grocery"/"food"/"pharmacy"),
not an integer id — see link_converter_helper.dart:62 sample link & route_helper.dart
dispatch (passes the raw query value). int.tryParse on a name always yields null, so
the "set module before fetch" branch the AC5 fix added never runs for a real
cross-module web/share deep link. Needs a name->moduleId resolve (ModuleModel list in
SplashController) before the fetch, OR fetch with an explicit moduleId header derived
from the link, OR (if links truly only ever carry int ids) fix the producer — but the
shipped sample link and the store-route branch both use the NAME, so the consumer must
map name->id.
